BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meditation in Asheville
UID:event_315469736@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260717T001637Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260719T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260719T114500
SUMMARY:Dealing with Difficult Emotions
DESCRIPTION:Meditation in Asheville: Meditation and Modern Buddhism\nDeali
 ng with Difficult Emotions with Modern Buddhism Teacher Jill Cagney\n\n**S
 undays 6/28-8/9 10:30am-11:45am**\nOverwhelmed by your feelings? Buddhist 
 psychology offers a time-tested\, powerful and healthy approach to dealing
  with painful\, challenging emotions. Each week\, we will apply these meth
 ods to states like craving\, anger\, jealousy\, and self-hatred. First\, w
 e need to recognize them\, learn how they work\, and accept ourselves for 
 where we are\, Next\, we can disempower them using special meditations. Fi
 nally\, we can envision and even experience a state of total freedom and r
 elease\, having transcended these difficult emotions.\nCost: $12 (free and
  online options for members)\n[Read More and Register](https://www.meditat
 ioninasheville.org/sunday-drop-in-meditation-class/)\n[Become a Member](ht
 tps://www.meditationinasheville.org/become-a-member/)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/meditationinasheville/events/31546973
 6/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260629T145246Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260629T145246Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meditation in Asheville
UID:event_315515620@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260717T001637Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260722T114500
SUMMARY:Making the Most of Difficult Situations
DESCRIPTION:Meditation in Asheville: Meditation and Modern Buddhism\nMakin
 g the Most of Difficult Situations with Modern Buddhism Teacher Sue Pepka\
 n\n**Sundays 5/17-6/14 10:30am-11:45am**\nDifficulties in our lives can st
 ir up fear\, frustration\, and discouragement-but they can also become the
  fuel for real inner growth. In this series of talks and guided meditation
 s\, we will explore the profound practice of transforming adversity into t
 he path. We will discover how to move beyond unhealthy emotional habits an
 d develop natural confidence\, inner flexibility\, and resilience. Learn t
 o respond differently to life's challenges and uncover a deeper peace of m
 ind—while strengthening your ability to support others.\n\nCost: $12 (fr
 ee and online options for members)\n[Read More and Register](https://www.m
 editationinasheville.org/wednesday-drop-in-meditation-class-asheville-nc/)
 \n[Become a Member](https://www.meditationinasheville.org/become-a-member/
 )
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/meditationinasheville/events/31551562
 0/
